  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;initially at rest on a smooth horizontal plane starts moving under the action of force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. In the process of its linear motion, the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> (as shown in figure) between the direction of force and horizontal varies as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is a constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the distance covered by the object from its initial position. The expression of kinetic energy of the object will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/01b39f2a-6cbf-4008-af64-51e019c28c14-9894258.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 157px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7fad4c6d-9244-4afa-8474-0022847ca6bc-9894258_2.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 259px;\" /></p><p>As seen in&nbsp;the free body diagram of the object, normal force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>, weight&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;and force in parallel and perpendicular directions are acting.</p><p>Using Newton&#39;s law of motion</p><p>Along horizontal direction,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ma</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Integrating the above relation, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Thus, kinetic energy of the object will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
